00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:38.710
So it's a, huge adjustment
and yet there's so much

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.913
to be done, It's like I'm not not busy.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.500
- And where are you
spending most of your time?

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.163
Is that around the virus work?

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:54.330
- Yes, that's, the our foundation works

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.330
on infectious diseases,
we are the biggest funder

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:01.360
of vaccine work, we understand,
how to make vaccines

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.760
in volume, we do the disease modeling.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.150
And so, the skills that we have,

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.590
understanding private
sector, being able to work

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:12.640
with governments, what
regulatory things should

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.670
be maintained for safety, and which ones,

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:20.873
because we've got to move so
fast, Should you go around?

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.940
and talking to leaders,
talking to Tony Fauci,

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:28.670
About Okay, how do we make
sure the public is seeing this

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:30.250
in the right way.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.840
We explain, why it takes
so long for a vaccine,

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:37.840
which is such a key thing
to.. until we have that,

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.630
We can open up a bit but

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.270
we won't go back completely to normal.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:47.270
And so we're orchestrating,
all of our partners around,

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:51.863
getting the testing right,
getting the drugs right,

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.840
and getting a vaccine
which will will bring us

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.970
to the end of this.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:01.570
- Yeah, now we're gonna
talk more about that.

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.400
And actually, the first
question I wanna surface

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.140
is from Facebook, Abid Sheikh,

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.540
and I think it's front
of mind for a lot of us.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.870
He writes Hello, since you predicted about

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:14.190
a similar outbreak in the 2015, Ted Talk,

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.730
how did you react to the news
about the Covid 19 pandemic?

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.630
And that he's referring to a famously for

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:22.650
anyone who doesn't know,
Bill made a talk in 2015,

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.160
that essentially was very prescient

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.660
of the situation we're in now.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.080
- Yeah, and I wrote a New England Journal

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.520
of Medicine article
that really went through

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:34.580
the specific things, like
high speed diagnostics

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:39.240
and vaccine platforms
that we needed to fund.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.840
This is certainly a case
where being able to say,

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.970
I told you so is not at all gratifying,

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:48.860
because this is a horrific
disaster and in my lifetime,

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:52.140
whether it's health or
economics or just uncertainty

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.290
for people, there's nothing like this.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:05:00.290
And the goal there, was to
get governments to step up,

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:04.850
so that you could easily
make a new RNA vaccine

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:09.850
or you'd have, the testing
capacity very, very rapidly.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:14.090
I'm sure that because
this is so widespread

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:18.020
that next time we will have
made those investments,

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:22.920
but it's unfortunate that,
very little got done in

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.910
our foundation, Wellcome Trust,

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:28.950
a few others did fund
work along these lines,

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:30.513
but not enough.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.823
And, you know, so here, here we are.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:38.520
- And give us a sense of
where we are right now.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.870
And we could talk a little bit about maybe

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:42.550
what could or should have
happened, but where are we now?

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:45.120
What's your analysis,
how bad is the situation

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.880
in the US rest of world,
how close are we to peak?

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.843
How's it's gonna play out over
the next few weeks or months?

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:55.760
- Yeah so, the concept
of exponential growth,

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.000
is not that intuitive to people,

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.470
but when you have this human

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:03.800
to human transmissible respiratory virus,

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.190
it creates exponential growth,
that is each case leads

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:12.190
to, say two or more cases,
and so, if we haven't changed

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:18.980
our behavior, there's no doubt
the majority of people would

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.420
be infected, and you'd
get this huge overload

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:26.420
of the medical system, and
literally millions of deaths.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:30.560
The reactions, whenever
you're gonna stop something

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:33.220
that's exponential, the sooner you act,

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:35.690
the better because then
you can act in a way that

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:39.210
you don't overload your hospital systems.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:42.030
And you can treat the
cases very, very well.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:44.860
Testing is key to know where's the spread,

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.950
and to inform people that they need

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.270
to really isolate themselves, the tests

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:54.160
the PCR test can actually
see the virus before

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:55.540
you're symptomatic, before you would

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.030
be transmitting to people.

00:06:57.030 --> 00:07:00.970
And so, if we had had the
testing right prioritized,

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:05.373
that would help with this,
with the social isolation,

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:09.350
by the end of the month
with any luck, we'll start

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:12.640
to see the curve level off.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:16.700
And then another month, the
number of cases would come down.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:19.200
And you could get to a point where,

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.030
because you are targeting the testing

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:25.260
and giving quick results,
that will do start

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:29.870
to open up in a way like
China has where kids do go

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:32.180
to school, people go back to their jobs,

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:36.020
it's not normal that they
don't do sports events

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:40.120
or big gatherings, that
will wait until the vaccine

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:43.410
but we'd like, if things go well,

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:45.800
and the numbers will
drive it. we'd like to see

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:50.800
thatability to open up somewhat
by ideally early summer.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.670
- And as we are all seeing evidence

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.170
that the social distancing is working that

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:56.950
we are on track to peak,
in the next few weeks

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:01.550
and then, get to maybe a more
a better state by the end

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:04.110
of, I guess would be by the end of May.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:08.113
- Well, China had in Hebei
Province, over 80,000 cases

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.850
and so that's the model
where they intervened

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:14.950
in a very dramatic way,

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:17.800
they enforced their
quarantine very strongly.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:20.270
They did their contact
tracing, they used the testing,

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.900
people would get testing
results very quickly,

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:24.980
and it was the right people.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:28.370
They are now, able to open up.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:32.680
South Korea had reasonable
number of cases,

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:36.420
but they did the testing did the tracing,

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:41.160
and so now they are in
the situation where,

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.330
they've definitely bent the curve.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.160
There are a few countries like Taiwan

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:48.260
who did all the right
things and never allowed

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:49.700
the large numbers to develop.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.343
That unfortunately for most countries,

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:56.820
we can't go back and
change the fact we missed

00:08:56.820 --> 00:09:01.190
that early opportunity, but
they, there are communities

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:04.610
where we are starting
to see the numbers peak

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.710
because of that social isolation,
so that's the first step

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:10.920
is that peak, but you don't open up until

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:14.070
they're in absolute, way below,

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:16.713
like a factor of five
below where they are today.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:21.530
- Wow, and just from us, I
don't know from either economic

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:23.310
or a scientific point of view,

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.760
why do we see this disparity in testing,

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:27.180
or even the types of tests?

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:30.240
In the US right now, even if
you're kind of lucky enough

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:32.990
to get a test, so to speak, it
could still take several days

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:35.240
to get a result, while
you know, I heard stories

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.810
in Taiwan three months
ago, you get your results

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.260
before you leave the airport?

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:43.410
- Yeah, the very sensitive test is

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:47.540
the Polymerase Chain
Reaction PCR, where you make

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:51.360
the primer specifically for this virus.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.480
It's an amazing test and there's a lot

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:57.100
of machines out there, in
commercial labs, academic centers,

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:01.760
public health labs, that we were slow

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:03.950
to get them all going, even today,

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.090
we're not completely
taken advantage of that.

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:09.690
If you make sure you're
testing healthcare workers,

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:12.030
you don't let the queue to get very long,

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:15.760
you're testing contacts and
people who test positive,

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.240
that really is guiding individual behavior

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:19.910
and the abroad behavior.

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:22.290
And so that in the US,
we actually have more

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.990
of those machines per
capita than South Korea

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.430
or anyone else.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:29.700
So, it should be possible.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:33.380
There isn't a set of criteria
though, that stops somebody

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:36.540
who's not symptomatic from
say, getting in the queue

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:38.170
and testing themselves every day

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:41.210
just 'cause they're worried,
versus that healthcare worker.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:45.260
And so, we do need to bring
a sense of prioritization

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:49.330
and not let these queues
mean, it's taking too long

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.653
to get the results back.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:53.530
- Are you hopeful that
that's going to change over

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:54.363
the next couple of weeks?

00:10:54.363 --> 00:10:57.483
- Yes, well, there's a lot
of discussion about it,

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:01.260
the notion of okay,

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.820
does the federal level
really jump into that?

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:08.820
Which agency, has the right
expertise to be able to do that?

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:13.600
And so, that I think is likely

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:16.103
to improve in the weeks ahead.

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.440
- And your prediction of hitting a peak

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:21.050
in the country in a few weeks,

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:23.350
one question I've been curious about it,

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:26.630
places like California I know
in Seattle and Washington,

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:29.990
we've been in some form
of stay at home policy,

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:31.820
stay in place policy, lockdown policy

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:34.540
for about three weeks now,
and the quarantine time

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:37.310
is typically two weeks,
why aren't we seeing

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:40.503
the peak cases sooner, why
is it taking so much time?

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:46.520
- Well, there's the league
of, once you do the shutdown,

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:52.140
you need to go, at least maybe
two infection periods before

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.660
you'd really expect to
see things going down.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:59.570
Also, we weren't doing
enough testing, and so,

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:02.650
now we're seeing, a higher percentage

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:04.433
of what's actually out there.

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:08.780
And, but the actual the
numbers for California

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:12.030
and Washington are very hopeful,

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:13.770
the New York numbers continue to go up.

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:17.190
We have cities with explosive
growth, like Detroit,

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:21.523
New Orleans, but the
there are early signs,

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:26.860
that our, our changes
have made a difference.

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:30.460
Our lockdown is not as extreme
as what they did in China,

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:33.370
but it should be enough in the places

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:37.270
where there's strong
adherence, to get to that peak.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:40.280
And so I'd say, we'll see in some locals

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:46.150
in the next few weeks, we'll
see that, but for the country,

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:48.263
at best, it would be the end of the month.

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:50.810
- And what's your sense of why New York

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:53.910
has had such a tough situation?

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.690
They're in a lockdown situation now,

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:57.810
is it just the nature
of the density of people

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.000
or is there something else going on there?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.010
- Well, the international
travel into New York

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.880
is more than anywhere
else, the density is more

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:11.760
than anywhere else,and these
things, there's some degree

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:14.640
of bad luck, when you're
dealing with the exponential

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.840
just a few cases here at the front

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:20.780
of the exponential can
drive a big separation

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.770
between place A in place B.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:27.130
And, the governor, there is stepping up

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:32.070
and getting the models
to help him understand

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:34.670
what's going on, enforcing

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:37.293
their lockdown in a pretty serious way.

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:43.390
So hopefully, the deaths are
another lagging indicator,

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:45.290
because those are people

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:47.870
who were infected 18 to 20 days earlier.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:51.940
But, we really hope that New York peaks

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:55.110
because they are, near the breaking point

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.513
for their medical system.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:59.750
- And you're one of the world's experts

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:01.270
and you've worked with
many of the world's experts

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:02.940
on things like vaccines,
obviously, there's a lot

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:03.773
of talk about a vaccine,

